          "With the default box-sizing: content-box, the width and height properties set only the content area dimensions. Padding and border widths are added on top, so an element with width: 200px, padding: 20px, and border: 5px actually occupies 250px horizontally. This behavior surprises many beginners and causes layout overflow issues.",
