          "Web performance directly affects user experience, conversion rates, and search engine rankings. Google's Core Web Vitals measure three key metrics: Largest Contentful Paint (LCP, loading speed, target under 2.5s), Interaction to Next Paint (INP, responsiveness, target under 200ms), and Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS, visual stability, target under 0.1). Monitoring these metrics guides optimization priorities.",
          "Minimize the critical rendering path by reducing the number and size of resources the browser must download and parse before displaying content. Place CSS in the head so styles arrive early, defer non-critical JavaScript with the defer attribute, and eliminate render-blocking resources where possible. Inline critical above-the-fold CSS for the fastest first paint.",
          "Image optimization has outsized impact because images typically account for the largest portion of page weight. Use modern formats like WebP and AVIF that offer better compression than JPEG and PNG. Serve appropriately sized images with srcset and sizes attributes so mobile devices download smaller files. Lazy-load below-the-fold images with loading=\"lazy\" to defer off-screen downloads.",
          "Minify and compress text assets: minification removes whitespace and comments from CSS and JavaScript files, while gzip or Brotli compression reduces transfer size by 60-80%. Enable compression on the web server and use build tools (esbuild, Terser, cssnano) to minify assets during deployment. Concatenating many small files into fewer requests also reduces HTTP overhead.",
          "Caching strategies reduce repeat load times. Set Cache-Control headers to tell browsers and CDNs how long to store assets. Use content hashing in filenames (app.a1b2c3.js) for long-term caching of static assets, since the hash changes only when content changes. HTML files typically use shorter cache durations or no-cache to ensure users receive updates.",
          "Measure before optimizing using Lighthouse in Chrome DevTools, WebPageTest, or real-user monitoring tools. Profile JavaScript execution in the Performance panel to find long tasks blocking the main thread. Avoid premature optimization—identify the actual bottlenecks through measurement, then apply targeted fixes rather than applying every technique indiscriminately."
