          "The history of robotics spans from early industrial arms in manufacturing plants to modern autonomous drones, surgical assistants, and warehouse mobile robots. Early robots focused on repetitive, dangerous, or precision tasks that humans could not perform consistently at scale. Today, robotics applications extend into agriculture, logistics, healthcare, exploration, defense, and consumer products such as vacuum cleaners and educational kits.",
