          "Global planners compute coarse routes over occupancy grids, topological graphs, or road networks. Algorithms such as A*, Dijkstra, and RRT* find paths that avoid static obstacles and respect kinematic constraints. Local planners or trajectory trackers follow the global route while reacting to dynamic obstacles detected in real time by lidar, radar, or vision.",
